<p class="post-intro">I arrived in the UK ten years ago, and from the very first day I wanted to do business here and establish a company 🚀</p>

<p>After setting up the basics of life, I finally registered Petiole Pro, and it felt like the job is done 😂. Oh, what a naïve happiness before the sharp question: so what's next with my innovation &amp; business?</p>

<p>Once the company was alive, I discovered a whole new mountain of business problems to solve. And, as you might remember, back in 2017 there were no AI assistants around to help :)))</p>

<h2>The one thing that never changes</h2>

<p>But there has always-always-always been one thing in business. Whether a thousand years ago, in Medieval times, in the pre-Internet era, or in today's AI-powered world.</p>

<p>It's called <strong>"business networks"</strong> 🤝</p>

<p>So I'm not the first, and definitely not the last, to find value in them and use them to grow my innovation beyond just my head.</p>

<h2>Why am I writing this today?</h2>

<p>Because I want to invite you to an online event by <strong>Innovate UK Business Connect</strong> 👇 This is the organisation that helped me a lot.</p>

<p>They are</p>
<ul class="post-steps">
  <li><strong>(a)</strong> connected to ALL the business networks in the UK, and</li>
  <li><strong>(b)</strong> systematically helping innovators become part of the ecosystem (even me: a foreigner, an immigrant with a strong Eastern European accent :))</li>
</ul>

<p>Jumping back to my story: I didn't go to Innovate UK Business Connect straight away. Not on day one, no.</p>

<p>However, I think if I had, my journey would have been faster and more productive, without a few years of thinking-overthinking-rethinking.</p>

<p>And, frankly speaking, I was not moving my business forward during that period...</p>

